                <pb facs="0344" n="226" sameAs="frus:frus1928v02/pg226"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/9964: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >MacMurray</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-05-18T15:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">May 18, 1928—3
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>163. Your telegram 360, May 17, 4 p.m., has arrived since the sending of my
                    telegram 162, May 18, 1 p.m. I am in entire agreement <pb facs="0345" n="227"
                        xml:id="pg227"/> with you and Generals Butler and Castner. Your view of the
                    situation is, in my opinion, correct.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
